- The base case is when `n` is less than or equal to 1, in which case the function returns `n`.
- For all other values of `n`, the function calls itself recursively to find the (n-1)th and (n-2)th Fibonacci numbers, and then returns the sum of these two numbers.
- The `main()` function prompts the user to enter a value for `n`, calls the `fibonacci()` function with this value, and prints the result to the console.

Note that this program uses recursion, which can be slow for large values of `n`. For better performance, you can use an iterative approach instead.<|end_of_text|>

